Third-party software linked into PlayFX
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

chiaki-ng (third_party/chiaki-ng): the Remote Play protocol implementation (libchiaki).
  AGPL-3.0-only, with an exception for linking OpenSSL. https://github.com/streetpea/chiaki-ng
  Bundled by chiaki-ng and statically linked:
    curl          curl license (MIT/X derivative)     https://curl.se
    nanopb        zlib license                        https://github.com/nanopb/nanopb
    Jerasure      BSD 3-Clause                        https://github.com/tsuraan/Jerasure
    GF-Complete   BSD 3-Clause                        https://github.com/ceph/gf-complete

Statically linked from Homebrew at build time:
    OpenSSL 3     Apache License 2.0                  https://www.openssl.org
    Opus          BSD 3-Clause                        https://opus-codec.org
    json-c        MIT                                 https://github.com/json-c/json-c
    miniupnpc     BSD 3-Clause                        https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp
    libevent      BSD 3-Clause                        https://libevent.org

The desktop app also includes Tauri, React, Effect and other npm and Cargo packages under their
own licenses (mostly MIT and Apache-2.0); each package carries its license in its distribution.
